# peekseed -- configuration template
#
# Copy to `.env` (or export these variables) before running. A real environment
# variable wins over this file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The authoritative service config is the deployment env file
# (deploy/env/peekseed.env, mode 0600); this template is for a source checkout.
# API keys belong only in that env file, never in this one.

# --- data folders (both required) -----------------------------------------
# Absolute, existing directories; there are no fallbacks (no ./workspace and no
# ~/peekseed). A missing value stops the program with a clear error.
#
# PEEKSEED_HOME: private state (config, datasets, history, jobs, uploads, logs,
# env/venv + locks). `peekseed init` creates and hardens it to 0700.
# PEEKSEED_HOME=/abs/path/livefield/.peekseed
#
# PEEKSEED_SHARED_DIR: shared with peelfeed -- sources/<sha256>/<name>.pdf (the
# ONE stored copy of each uploaded PDF) and peels/<peel_id>/.
# PEEKSEED_SHARED_DIR=/abs/path/livefield/shared

# Explicit dotenv file; otherwise .env is read from the working directory.
# PEEKSEED_ENV_FILE=./.env

# --- server ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Loopback by default. Before exposing the app beyond this machine, set a
# shared token and pin the Host/Origin names you use: mutating /api/* calls
# then require the token, and mismatched Host/Origin values are rejected.
# PEEKSEED_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PEEKSEED_PORT=8030
# PEEKSEED_TOKEN=
# PEEKSEED_ALLOWED_HOSTS=box.lan,192.168.1.10:8030

# --- local models (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Machine-local launch scripts live in a JSON file (the deployment keeps it at
# deploy/env/local_models.json). Unset means "no local models".
# PEEKSEED_LOCAL_MODELS_FILE=/abs/path/deploy/env/local_models.json

# --- model links -----------------------------------------------------------
# Links are stored in $PEEKSEED_HOME/config/links.json and edited in the UI.
# There is no env seeding of links: a link names the environment variable that
# holds its API key (`api_key_env`, matching ^PEEKSEED_[A-Z0-9_]+_API_KEY$), and
# the key itself lives only in the service env file. The UI cannot enter keys.

# --- peelfeed: the extraction engine (optional; CLI only) ------------------
# Uploads and file management work without peelfeed; extraction (Extract,
# review, building an index from a corpus) runs the peelfeed CLI as a
# subprocess. The first run writes $PEEKSEED_HOME/config/peelfeed.json (0600)
# from these values; a real environment variable wins over the file and .env.
# There is no daemon, no base URL and no token: the seam is the command line.
#
# Preferred: absolute path to the peelfeed console script.
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_CLI=/abs/path/livefield/.peelfeed/env/venv/bin/peelfeed
# Fallback: absolute path to the peelfeed venv interpreter. peekseed runs
# `python -m peelfeed.cli` with PYTHONPATH=<repo> (derived from this path, or
# from PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_REPO when the path is elsewhere).
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_PYTHON=/abs/path/livefield/.peelfeed/env/venv/bin/python
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_REPO=/abs/path/peelfeed
# peelfeed itself requires a home (venvs + model caches) and the same shared
# dir; the peel root is always $PEEKSEED_SHARED_DIR/peels.
# PEELFEED_HOME=/abs/path/livefield/.peelfeed
# PEELFEED_SHARED_DIR=/abs/path/livefield/shared   # must equal PEEKSEED_SHARED_DIR
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_ENABLED=1        # 0 = explicitly disable extraction
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_TIMEOUT=7200     # seconds; ingest/rebuild may run for a while
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_POLL=2           # UI status poll interval, seconds
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_LLM_MODE=off     # off | review | aggressive
# PEEKSEED_PEELFEED_CHUNK_PROFILE=default

# --- answer + research knobs ----------------------------------------------
# PEEKSEED_ASK_MAX_CHUNKS=8
# PEEKSEED_ASK_MAX_CHARS=6000
# PEEKSEED_ASK_MAX_TOKENS=4096
# PEEKSEED_ASK_TEMPERATURE=0.2
# PEEKSEED_RERANK_POOL=20
# PEEKSEED_RERANK_BATCH=8

# --- agent / research mode (off by default) -------------------------------
# PEEKSEED_AGENT=1
# PEEKSEED_AGENT_MAX_STEPS=6
# PEEKSEED_AGENT_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=12
# PEEKSEED_AGENT_WALL_SEC=240
